+# Epic RC2 Context: Reference-Check Foundation & Viewing Trigger
+
+<!-- Compiled from planning artifacts. Edit freely. Regenerate with compile-epic-context if planning docs change. -->
+
+## Goal
+
+Establish the system of record for reference checking: the `reference_call` lifecycle table, the Art 21 objection evidence log, the application `viewed` status, and the trigger that auto-creates checks when a viewing is marked done. After this epic the platform knows who to chase and when to start — but sends nothing yet (the sweep in RC3 owns all sends).
+
+## Stories
+
+- Story RC2.1: `reference_call` + `reference_objection_log` schema, enums, indexes, shared types/codecs
+- Story RC2.2: `viewed` application status end to end (enum, codecs, stepper UI)
+- Story RC2.3: trigger on `viewed` + manual start / skip APIs, creation audit
+
+## Requirements & Constraints
+
+- One migration creates both tables, both enums, and all indexes; companion migrations follow the repo's one-purpose-per-migration precedent. New `notification_type` values (`reference_completed`, `reference_unreachable`, `reference_objected`, `reference_declined`) ship with RC2.1 so later emitting stories have their types.
+- Amendments binding this epic (from the epics doc's A-register): no `correction_token` column or applicant correction route (landlord-driven correction, A1); `draft_answers` JSONB for referee autosave (A2); form-link TTL is 10 days (A3); attestation choice recorded per application (A4, RC1's column — RC2 only consumes it); trigger is `viewed`, not shortlist (A5); `'skipped'` status exists, occupies its live slot, and re-enables to `queued` (A6); takeover modelled as `taken_over_at` (A7); form decline = `refused` terminal with `reference_declined` notification (A8).
+- `reference_call` rows are created `queued` with `next_attempt_at = now()` and the immutable `contact_*` snapshot; **nothing is sent at creation**. Auto-create is suppressed when `reference_contact_choice = 'declined'`; pre-v1 (NULL) applications DO trigger. Double-trigger must not duplicate rows (guarded INSERT against the live-slot partial unique index).
+- Objection is a sticky short-circuit: `reference_objection_log` is written at objection time by a single writer, has NO foreign keys, and must survive deletion of both parents (Art 21 evidence).
+- Retention integrates with the application schedule via `retention_class` + `purge_after` on both new tables; application-level CASCADE is the v1 enforcement path.
+- Lifecycle events write `audit_log` rows (entity_type `reference_call`).
+
+## Technical Decisions
+
+- `status`/`outcome` are PG enums (`reference_call_status` incl. `'skipped'` and v2-reserved values; `reference_call_outcome` incl. the §6.4 additions `unreachable`, `form_completed`, `manual_recorded`). `ref_slot`, `owner_label`, `channel`, `retention_class` are TEXT+CHECK — an owned deviation keeping DDL in lockstep with the cross-repo JSON contract.
+- Live-row uniqueness: partial unique index on `(application_id, ref_slot, owner_label)` excluding every terminal status but NOT `'skipped'`. Unique partial index on `form_token`. Plus sweep (`next_attempt_at`), application, contact-phone (cross-application fraud check), and purge indexes.
+- `updated_at` via the repo's existing generic trigger-function pattern. RLS auto-enables via event trigger; zero policies are written (deliberate repo posture, service-role-only access).
+- Squirrel codegen needs a DB carrying the new migration — use the local Docker test DB (`make test-db-up` runs migrations), never staging, and point `DATABASE_URL` at it for `gleam run -m squirrel`.
+- Squirrel limitations (canonical): no timestamptz params (pass TEXT, cast in SQL), lowercase `::text` casts only.
+- `reference_call` FK to `application` is ON DELETE CASCADE; the immutable `contact_*` snapshot records who was actually contacted (corrections land in `corrected_email`/`corrected_phone`, snapshot never overwritten).
+- Shared package owns the types + JSON codecs for status/outcome (compilation-boundary convention); enum variant tests use the enumerate-all-variants round-trip pattern. Internal-only fields (`form_token`, `objection_detail.payload_ref`) never leave the server.
+- Terminal-no-content rows still get a `result` JSONB (outcome + attempts, null verification) so v2 re-score reads uniformly; `fraud_signals` is denormalised to its own column.
+- Migration header comments follow house style (intent + rationale prose); enum additions use `ALTER TYPE ... ADD VALUE IF NOT EXISTS` in their own tiny migration (a newly added enum value can't be referenced in the same transaction).
+
+## Cross-Story Dependencies
+
+- RC2.1 is the schema foundation: RC2.3 creates rows against it, RC4.1's payload contract may start as soon as RC2.1 lands, and RC3's sweep/token work builds on its columns.
+- RC2.3 depends on RC2.2's `viewed` status and on RC1.1's `reference_contact_choice` column (sibling epic RC1 runs in parallel on a different branch — `shared/src/shared/application.gleam` and the `consent_type` enum are THEIRS; RC2 stories must not touch them).
+- RC2.1 must NOT create the `consent_type` value or application capture columns (RC1.1's migrations) and must NOT add `'viewed'` to `application_status` (RC2.2's migration).
