+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** AI reference-checking v1 has no system of record. Every later story (trigger, sweep, form, panel) needs the `reference_call` lifecycle table, the Art 21 objection evidence log, their enums/indexes, and typed Gleam access — built exactly on the agreed contract.
+
+**Approach:** One schema migration per architecture §4.1 *as amended by the epics doc's A-register*, one tiny notification-type enum migration, Squirrel SQL + generated CRUD primitives in a new `server/src/reference_checks/` module, and shared enum types + JSON codecs with round-trip tests.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Migration SQL follows architecture §4.1 *as amended*: status enum gains `'skipped'` (A6); outcome enum gains `'unreachable'`, `'form_completed'`, `'manual_recorded'` (§6.4); add `draft_answers` JSONB (A2) and `taken_over_at TIMESTAMPTZ` (A7); **no `correction_token` column or index** (A1).
+- Live-row partial unique index on `(application_id, ref_slot, owner_label)` excludes every terminal status (`form_completed`,`unreachable`,`refused`,`objected`,`manual_recorded`,`failed`,`completed`,`partial`) but NOT `'skipped'` (A6 — a skipped row occupies its slot).
+- `ref_slot`/`owner_label`/`channel`/`retention_class` = TEXT+CHECK (owned deviation); `status`/`outcome` = PG enums; `updated_at` via the existing generic `update_updated_at_column()` trigger (ai_analysis pattern); retention_class CHECK set = `('referee_submission','objection_evidence','attempt_metadata')` (§9.3), defaults `'referee_submission'` / `'objection_evidence'`.
+- `reference_objection_log` has **no foreign keys** (survives both parent deletions); purge partial index on both tables; unique partial index on `form_token`; sweep (`next_attempt_at`), `application_id`, `contact_phone` indexes.
+- Four `notification_type` values via `ALTER TYPE ... ADD VALUE IF NOT EXISTS` in their own tiny migration (20260423100001 precedent): `reference_completed`, `reference_unreachable`, `reference_objected`, `reference_declined`.
+- House migration header-comment style (intent + rationale prose); RLS auto-enables via existing event trigger — write zero policy content.
+- Shared codecs follow the `application.gleam`/`error_code` pattern (encode/from_string, total inverse); tests enumerate ALL variants for round-trip.
+- Squirrel limitations: timestamptz params passed as TEXT + `::timestamptz` cast; enum params as TEXT + `::enum` cast; JSONB params `::jsonb`.
+
+**Ask First:** any deviation from architecture §4.1-as-amended (column rename, dropped index, extra column); touching RC1.1's files.
+
+**Never:** no `correction_token`; no applicant-facing correction routes; no RLS policies; no edits to `shared/src/shared/application.gleam`, `consent_type`, or `application_status` (sibling minion owns RC1.1; RC2.2 owns `'viewed'`); no sends/sweep logic; no migrations against staging or production — local Docker test DB only.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Fresh reset | `scripts/reset-test-db.sh` over all migrations | Both enums, both tables, all indexes, trigger exist; 4 notification values added | Migration error aborts with ON_ERROR_STOP |
+| Live-slot uniqueness | Two non-terminal rows, same (application_id, ref_slot, owner_label) | Second insert rejected by partial unique index | DB unique violation |
+| Skipped occupies slot | One row `status='skipped'`, insert same slot trio | Rejected (skipped NOT in terminal exclusion) | DB unique violation |
+| Terminal frees slot | Prior row terminal (e.g. `unreachable`), insert same slot trio | Insert succeeds (substitution path) | N/A |
+| Objection log orphan | Row with reference_call_id/application_id set, parents deleted | Log row survives (no FKs) | N/A |
+| Codec round-trip | Every status/outcome variant | `from_string(encode(v)) == v` for all 14 + 15 variants | Test fails on missing arm |
+
