+## Spec Change Log
+
+## Design Notes
+
+- Enum value order: `'skipped'` placed directly after `'queued'` in `reference_call_status` (lifecycle adjacency; PG enum order has no v1 consumer).
+- `insert_reference_call` deliberately takes no `next_attempt_at` param — creation always stamps `now()` (FR-RC3); re-enable after skip is a later story's guarded update.
+- The objection-log schema test greps the migration *file* (audit_log_schema_test precedent) so DB-free CI pins the no-FK / no-correction_token invariants.
+- `form_token_expires_at` is a bare column — the 10-day TTL (A3) is a runtime policy of the token-issuing story (RC3.x), noted in the column comment.
+- **Squirrel nullability (learned during implementation):** squirrel types cast expressions as non-`Option` (and cannot codegen timestamptz results at all), so nullable non-text columns are selected as `COALESCE(x::text, '')` — '' is the absent marker, mirroring the house `NULLIF($n,'')` input convention. Plain nullable TEXT columns stay `Option(String)`. The existing `ai/sql.gleam` `completed_at::text` non-Option typing is a latent instance of this trap — do not copy it.
+- **Test-DB port deviation:** a sibling minion's container already bound 54321, so the local DB ran on 54322 (`docker run postgres:16-alpine` + `TEST_DB_PORT=54322 scripts/reset-test-db.sh`); Squirrel and integration tests pointed at 54322. Same migrations-from-reset semantics as `make test-db-up`.
+- **Outcome constructors are `Outcome`-prefixed** in the shared module (Gleam constructor names are module-global; 7 collide with status variants). `from_string` helpers are total with documented fallbacks (application.gleam precedent); `*_decoder()` fails on unknown strings (ai_analysis.gleam precedent).
+
